\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs36\b 6. Quick Start: Adding Your First Calendar\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 {\b New to Delphi? Here are the key terms:}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 \'95\tab A {\b component} is a reusable building block you drag onto a form from the Tool Palette.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 \'95\tab A {\b property} is a setting you can change in the Object Inspector or in code.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 \'95\tab An {\b event} is code that runs automatically when something happens (for example, when the user clicks a date).\par

\pard\sb120\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b Step-by-step\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 1.\tab Start Delphi and create a new VCL Forms Application ({\b File > New > VCL Forms Application}).\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 2.\tab In the Tool Palette, find the {\b KingCalendar} section. If you do not see it, re-check the installation steps in Section 5.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 3.\tab Double-click {\b TKingCalendar} to place it on your form.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 4.\tab In the Object Inspector, change properties such as {\cf3\f1\fs20 CellColor\cf1\f0\fs22 }, {\cf3\f1\fs20 TitleColor\cf1\f0\fs22 }, and {\cf3\f1\fs20 Font\cf1\f0\fs22 } to customise the appearance.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 5.\tab To respond when the user clicks a date, switch to the {\b Events} tab of the Object Inspector and double-click the {\cf3\f1\fs20 OnClick\cf1\f0\fs22 } event. Add your code:\par

\pard\sb0\sa60\li720\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure TForm1.KingCalendar1Click(Sender: TObject);\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li720\cf3\f1\fs20 begin\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li720\cf3\f1\fs20   ShowMessage('You selected: ' + DateToStr(KingCalendar1.Date));\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li720\cf3\f1\fs20 end;\par

\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 6.\tab Press {\b F9} to run. Click any day to trigger your event.\par

\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 {\b Linking navigation controls:} To connect a {\cf3\f1\fs20 TMonthSpin\cf1\f0\fs22 }, {\cf3\f1\fs20 TKingNavigator\cf1\f0\fs22 }, or other companion control to your calendar, drop it on the form. It will automatically link to the first {\cf3\f1\fs20 TKingCalendar\cf1\f0\fs22  }it finds. If you have more than one calendar, set the control\'92s {\cf3\f1\fs20 CalendarLink\cf1\f0\fs22  }property in the Object Inspector, or right-click the control and choose {\b Attach to Calendar...} to pick from a list.\par

\pard\sb240\sa0\cf3\f0\fs16 ____________________________________________\par

\page

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs36\b 7. TKingCalendar \emdash  Main Calendar Component\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 TKingCalendar inherits from TCustomGrid and is the central component. It renders the month grid, handles day selection, blocked days, per-cell colors, and fires all calendar events. Every other component in the library links to a TKingCalendar instance.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 7.1  Properties\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 The following are the key properties you will use most often. Properties not listed here are inherited from TCustomGrid or TControl and behave in the standard Delphi way.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b Day\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property Day : Integer;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 The currently selected day of the month (1\endash 31). Changing this property updates the calendar display and fires OnDayChange.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b Month\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property Month : Integer;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 The currently selected month (1\endash 12). Changing this property navigates the calendar to that month and fires OnMonthChange.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b Year\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property Year : Integer;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 The currently selected year. Fires OnYearChange when changed.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b Date\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property Date : TDateTime;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 The full date as a TDateTime value. Setting this property updates Day, Month, and Year simultaneously. Read this property in your OnClick event to get the selected date.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b CellColor\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property CellColor : TColor;  { default: clBtnFace }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Background color of the day cells in the calendar grid.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b TitleColor\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property TitleColor : TColor;  { default: clBtnShadow }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Background color of the day-of-week header row.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b GridLineColor\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property GridLineColor : TColor;  { default: clBtnShadow }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Color of the lines drawn between cells. Set ShowGridLines to False to hide them entirely.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b ShowGridLines\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property ShowGridLines : Boolean;  { default: True }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Show or hide the grid lines between day cells.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b Highlight\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property Highlight : TColor;  { default: clHighlight }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Background color of the focused (selected) day cell.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b HighlightText\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property HighlightText : TColor;  { default: clHighlightText }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Text color of the selected day number.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b TodayColor\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property TodayColor : TColor;  { default: clWindowText }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Color used to draw today\'92s date number, making it stand out from other days.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b IsActive\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property IsActive : Boolean;  { default: True }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 When True, the focused day cell is highlighted using the Highlight color. Set to False to render all cells with the same background.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b TextPlacement\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property TextPlacement : TKingText;  { default: ktTopLeft }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Controls where the day number is drawn inside each cell. Options: ktCenter, ktTopLeft, ktTopRight, ktLowerLeft, ktLowerRight.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b ColorCellDay\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property ColorCellDay : Boolean;  { default: True }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 When True, day numbers are drawn using the colors defined by ColorSet1\endash ColorSet9 and TodayColor. When False, all day numbers use the calendar\'92s default Font color.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b Font\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property Font : TFont;  { default: Segoe UI, clWindowText }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Font used to draw the day numbers in the cells. For best VCL Style compatibility, set Font.Color to clWindowText rather than clBlack.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b TitleFont\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property TitleFont : TFont;  { default: Segoe UI, clWindowText }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Font used in the day-of-week header row.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b TextFont\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property TextFont : TFont;  { default: Segoe UI }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Font used to draw additional text lines inside cells (set via SetDateFlag).\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b DowNames\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property DowNames : TStrings;  { default: Sun Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 The seven day-of-week abbreviations shown in the header row. Change these to localise the calendar to any language.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b StartingDay\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property StartingDay : Integer;  { default: 0 (Sunday) }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 The first day of the week shown in the leftmost column. 0 = Sunday, 1 = Monday, and so on. Useful for European locales where Monday is the first day.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b BlockedBkGnd\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property BlockedBkGnd : TColor;  { default: clBtnFace }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Background color for days that have been blocked (disabled for selection).\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b BlockedFrGnd\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property BlockedFrGnd : TColor;  { default: clGrayText }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Text color for blocked day numbers.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b StyleName\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property StyleName : String;  { default: '' }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 The name of a VCL Style to use when painting this component. Leave blank to follow the application-wide active style. See Section 13 for details.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b ColorSet1 through ColorSet9\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property ColorSet1 : TColor;\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property ColorSet2 : TColor;\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 { ... through ColorSet9 }\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Nine user-defined colors used to color-code individual days. Assign a color set number (1\endash 9) to a day using SetDateFlag; the day number is then drawn in the corresponding ColorSet color.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b About\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 property About : String;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Read-only. Displays the library version number in the Object Inspector.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 7.2  Events\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b OnClick\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Fires when the user clicks any day cell. Read the Date property inside the handler to get the selected date.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b OnDayChange\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure(Sender: TObject; Day: Integer) of object;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Fires when the selected day changes. The new day number is passed as the Day parameter.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b OnMonthChange\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure(Sender: TObject; Month: Integer) of object;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Fires when the calendar navigates to a different month.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b OnYearChange\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure(Sender: TObject; Year: Integer) of object;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Fires when the calendar navigates to a different year.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b OnDateChange\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure(Sender: TObject; Date: TDateTime) of object;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Fires when the full date (day, month, or year) changes. This is the most convenient single event for most use cases.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b OnChange\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 General change notification. Fires after any date-related property changes.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b OnFlaggedDay\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Fires while the calendar is drawing a day that has a flag (appointment level > 0) set via SetDateFlag. Use this event to customise the painting of flagged days.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 7.3  Methods\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b SetDateFlag\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure SetDateFlag(nDay, Flag: Integer; Text: String);\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Assigns a color flag (1\endash 9, corresponding to ColorSet1\endash 9) and optional cell text to a specific day number in the current month. Call this to mark appointments, holidays, or any significant days.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b ClearDay\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure ClearDay(nDay: Integer);\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Removes the flag and text from a specific day.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b ClearAllDays\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure ClearAllDays;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Removes all flags and text from every day in the current month. Call this before repopulating the calendar when the month changes.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b AddColorBar\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure AddColorBar(nDay: Integer; nColor: TColor);\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Adds a colored bar inside a day cell. Useful for visually indicating appointments without replacing the day number.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b NextMonth / PrevMonth\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure NextMonth;\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure PrevMonth;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Navigates the calendar forward or back one month.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b NextYear / PrevYear\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure NextYear;\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure PrevYear;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Navigates the calendar forward or back one year.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b Today\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure Today;\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Jumps the calendar to today\'92s date.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b ColorDateRange\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure ColorDateRange(nStart, nEnd: Integer; nBack, nFore: TColor);\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Sets the background and foreground colors for all days in the range nStart through nEnd in the current month. Useful for highlighting date ranges such as vacations or booking periods.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b AcceptDropped\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 procedure AcceptDropped(X, Y, Tag: Integer; Text: String);\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Call this from your OnDragDrop event handler to place dropped text into the calendar cell at the given coordinates. See the DragDrop demo for a worked example.\par

\pard\sb240\sa0\cf3\f0\fs16 ____________________________________________\par

\page

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs36\b 8. TKingPopup \emdash  Popup Calendar\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 TKingPopup is a drop-down calendar control. The user clicks a button to reveal the calendar, selects a date, and the calendar closes automatically. It behaves similarly to a date-picker combo box.\par

\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 {\b Key properties:}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 Date : TDateTime\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 The currently selected date.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 DateFormat : String\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 Format string used to display the selected date in the edit area.\par

\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 {\b Key events:}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 OnChange\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 Fires when the user selects a new date. Read the Date property inside the handler.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 OnClose\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 Fires when the popup calendar closes.\par

\pard\sb240\sa0\cf3\f0\fs16 ____________________________________________\par

\page

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs36\b 9. TKingDateDialog \emdash  Date Picker Dialog\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 TKingDateDialog presents a modal dialog containing a calendar. The user selects a date and clicks OK or Cancel.\par

\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 {\b Typical usage:}\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 if KingDateDialog1.Execute then\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20   ShowMessage('Selected: ' + DateToStr(KingDateDialog1.Date));\par

\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 {\b Key properties:}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 Date : TDateTime\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 Set this before calling Execute to pre-select a date. Read it after Execute returns True.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 Caption : String\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 The dialog window title.\par

\pard\sb240\sa0\cf3\f0\fs16 ____________________________________________\par

\page

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs36\b 10. Navigation Controls\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 All navigation and companion controls share a common design: they have a {\cf3\f1\fs20 CalendarLink\cf1\f0\fs22 } property that you set to the {\cf3\f1\fs20 TKingCalendar\cf1\f0\fs22 } instance they should control. When you drop one of these controls onto a form that already contains a TKingCalendar, the CalendarLink is set automatically.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 10.1  TKingNavigator\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 A panel containing four arrow buttons: {\b previous month}, {\b next month}, {\b previous year}, {\b next year}. Drop it on a form, set {\cf3\f1\fs20 CalendarLink\cf1\f0\fs22 }, and it is immediately functional. No code required.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 10.2  TMonthBar\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 A row of twelve month-name buttons (Jan through Dec). Clicking a button navigates the linked calendar to that month. The current month button is automatically highlighted.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 10.3  TMonthSpin / TMonthCombo\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 TMonthSpin shows the current month name with up/down arrows to change it. TMonthCombo shows the same as a drop-down combo box. Both update the linked TKingCalendar when changed, and both update when the calendar navigates to a new month.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 10.4  TYearSpin / TYearCombo\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 Same concept as TMonthSpin/TMonthCombo, but for the year. TYearCombo shows a configurable range of years. Key property: {\cf3\f1\fs20 YearRange\cf1\f0\fs22 } (number of years before and after current year to include in the list).\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 10.5  TDaySpin / TDayCombo\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 Same concept for the day of the month. Automatically adjusts the maximum value for the number of days in the current month.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 10.6  TKingLabel / TKingWeekLabel\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 {\b TKingLabel} displays the linked calendar\'92s current date as a formatted string. Use the {\cf3\f1\fs20 DateFormat\cf1\f0\fs22 } property to control the format (e.g. {\cf3\f1\fs20 'dddd, mmmm d, yyyy'\cf1\f0\fs22 }).\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 {\b TKingWeekLabel} shows the ISO week number of the linked calendar\'92s current date. The label updates automatically whenever the calendar date changes.\par

\pard\sb240\sa0\cf3\f0\fs16 ____________________________________________\par

\page

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs36\b 11. Spin and Date Entry Controls\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 11.1  TKingDateSpin\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 An edit box with up/down spin arrows for entering a date value. The user can type a date directly or click the arrows to increment/decrement the currently focused date part (day, month, or year). Key properties:\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 Date : TDateTime\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 The current date value.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 DateFormat : String\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 Display format for the date (e.g. {\cf3\f1\fs20 'dd/mm/yyyy'\cf1\f0\fs22 }).\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 11.2  TKingTimeSpin\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 Same concept as TKingDateSpin but for time values. The user can tab between hours, minutes, and seconds and spin each field independently. Key property:\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 Time : TDateTime\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 The current time value.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 11.3  TKingMDYSpin\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 Combines three spin boxes in a single control: one each for month, day, and year. The user can edit each field independently. Useful when you want more explicit separated entry than a single formatted edit box provides.\par

\pard\sb240\sa0\cf3\f0\fs16 ____________________________________________\par

\page

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs36\b 12. Database Controls\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b 12.1  TDBKingDlg\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 TDBKingDlg is a database-aware version of TKingDateDialog. Link it to a dataset field by setting:\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 DataSource : TDataSource\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 The data source component connected to your dataset.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf3\f1\fs20 DataField : String\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\li1080\cf1\f0\fs22 The name of the date field in the dataset.\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 When the user picks a date and clicks OK, the field is updated automatically. The current field value is pre-selected when the dialog opens.\par

\pard\sb240\sa0\cf3\f0\fs16 ____________________________________________\par

\page

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs36\b 13. VCL Styles and Theming\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 KingCalendar v3.0 and later fully supports Delphi VCL Styles. All calendar drawing routes through Delphi\'92s {\cf3\f1\fs20 StyleServices\cf1\f0\fs22 } API, so the calendar automatically adapts to light and dark themes.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b Using the Application-Wide Style\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 Add {\cf3\f1\fs20 Vcl.Themes\cf1\f0\fs22 } and {\cf3\f1\fs20 Vcl.Styles\cf1\f0\fs22 } to your project\'92s uses clause. In your DPR file, before {\cf3\f1\fs20 Application.Run\cf1\f0\fs22 }, call:\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 TStyleManager.TrySetStyle('Glow');  // switch to a dark theme\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 The calendar will repaint automatically to match the new style.\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b Using Per-Component Styles\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 Set the {\cf3\f1\fs20 StyleName\cf1\f0\fs22 } property on any TKingCalendar to the name of a registered VCL Style:\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 KingCalendar1.StyleName := 'Glow';    // always paints in Glow\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 KingCalendar2.StyleName := '';         // follows app-wide style\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 The style must be registered in the application (either bundled via a styles package or loaded at startup). A blank StyleName means \'93follow whatever the application is currently using.\'94\par

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs28\b Tips for Dark Themes\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 \'95\tab Set {\cf3\f1\fs20 Font.Color\cf1\f0\fs22 }, {\cf3\f1\fs20 TitleFont.Color\cf1\f0\fs22 }, and {\cf3\f1\fs20 TextFont.Color\cf1\f0\fs22 } to {\cf3\f1\fs20 clWindowText\cf1\f0\fs22 } (not {\cf3\f1\fs20 clBlack\cf1\f0\fs22 }) so the style engine maps them to an appropriate light color in dark themes.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 \'95\tab Set {\cf3\f1\fs20 CellColor\cf1\f0\fs22 } to {\cf3\f1\fs20 clBtnFace\cf1\f0\fs22 } and {\cf3\f1\fs20 TitleColor\cf1\f0\fs22 } to {\cf3\f1\fs20 clBtnShadow\cf1\f0\fs22 } so they adapt with the theme.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sb0\sa80\cf1\f0\fs22 \'95\tab Avoid hard-coded color values (e.g. {\cf3\f1\fs20 RGB(0,0,0)\cf1\f0\fs22 }) for any element that should change with the theme.\par

\pard\sb240\sa0\cf3\f0\fs16 ____________________________________________\par

\page

\pard\sb240\sa120\cf2\f0\fs36\b 14. Demos\par
\pard\sb0\sa160\cf1\f0\fs22 The repository includes demo projects demonstrating the key features of the library. Each demo is available for Delphi 10.2, 10.3, 10.4, and 13. Open the {\cf3\f1\fs20 .dpr\cf1\f0\fs22 } file in Delphi, ensure KingCalendar is installed, and press F9 to run.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b KingCal Demo\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 Demos\Delphi13\Demo\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 The main feature showcase. Demonstrates cell coloring, text in cells, font and color customisation, navigation controls, and a VCL Style selector drop-down so you can see the calendar under multiple themes.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b NavEmpl\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 Demos\Delphi13\NavEmpl\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Demonstrates linking TKingCalendar to TKingNavigator, TMonthSpin, TYearSpin, TMonthBar, TKingLabel, and TKingWeekLabel. Useful if you want to build a navigation bar around the calendar.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b PickDate\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 Demos\Delphi13\PickDate\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Shows how to use TKingDateDialog and TKingPopup to pick a date and return it to a form.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b DragDrop\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 Demos\Delphi13\DragDrop\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Demonstrates drag-and-drop of text from a list box into calendar cells, using the AcceptDropped method.\par

\pard\sb120\sa40\cf2\f0\fs24\b StartDay\par
\pard\sb0\sa60\li360\cf3\f1\fs20 Demos\Delphi13\Startday\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\li360\cf1\f0\fs22 Shows the StartingDay property in action, allowing the user to switch the first day of the week at runtime.\par

\pard\sb240\sa0\cf3\f0\fs16 ____________________________________________\par

